l characteristics and deadline pressure into a monetary cost model that guides scheduling decisions.\nL65: Our evaluation shows that SkyNomad achieves 1.25–3.96$\\times$ cost savings in real cloud deployments and performs within 10% cost differences of an optimal policy in simulation, while consistently meeting deadlines.\nL536:   * [55] Sangho Yi, Derrick Kondo, and Artur Andrzejak. Reducing costs of spot instances via checkpointing in the Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud. In 2012 IEEE 3rd International Conference on Cloud Computing (CLOUD), pages 236–243. IEEE, 2010.\nL537:   * [56] Chengliang Zhang, Minchen Yu, Wei Wang, and Feng Yan. Mark: Exploiting cloud services for cost-effective, slo-aware machine learning inference serving. In 2019 USENIX Annual Technical Conference (USENIX ATC 19), pages 1049–1062. USENIX Association, 2019.\nL538:   * [57] Yanli Zhao, Andrew Gu, Rohan Varma, Liang Luo, Chien-Chin Huang, Min Xu, Less Wright, Hamid Shojanazeri, Myle Ott, Sam Shleifer, Alban Desmaison, Can Balioglu, Pritam Damania, Bernard Nguyen, Geeta Chauhan, Yuchen Hao, and Shen Li. Pytorch fsdp: Experiences on scaling fully sharded data parallel. Proceedings of the VLDB Endowment, 16(12):3848–3860, 2023.\nL539: Experimental support, please cite132†view the build logs for errors. Generated by cite133†L A T E xml†math.nist.gov .\nL540: ## Instructions for reporting errors\nL541: \nL542: We are continuing to improve HTML versions of papers, and your feedback helps enhance accessibility and mobile support. To report errors in the HTML that will help us improve conversion and rendering, choose any of the methods listed below:\nL543: \nL544:   * Click the \"Report Issue\" () button, located in the page header.\nL545: \nL546: Tip: You can select the relevant text first, to include it in your report.\nL547: Our team has already identified cite134†the following issues†github.com . We appreciate your time reviewing and reporting rendering errors we may not have found yet. Yo